From a4c2a7674af5f3daa963f80686fae8cc372e48b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:20:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] svg: add the common SVG element interfaces

Every SVG element except <svg> and <image> was created as a plain SVGElement, and
interface objects such as SVGAElement, SVGPathElement or SVGUseElement did not exist.
Pages that branch on them failed outright: crates.io's router evaluates
`el instanceof SVGAElement` on every click and threw a ReferenceError, and NYT does
similar checks.

Element creation now produces the interface Chrome uses for a, g, defs, symbol, use,
switch, foreignObject, the basic shapes and path (through SVGGeometryElement), the text
family, title/desc/metadata, gradients and stop, pattern, marker, clipPath, mask and
filter, with the same prototype chains. Interfaces without members of their own are
generated by a macro in svg/mod.rs. SVGAElement (href, target) and SVGUseElement (href)
expose SVGAnimatedString, with href falling back to xlink:href as SVGURIReference
specifies. Geometry and length members (getTotalLength, SVGAnimatedLength, ...) are
not implemented yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
